      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "You will need to go a long way to find a weaker TAB maiden than this. MADAME PETITE (8) started second favourite on debut last start over this distance at Yarra Valley but failed to pass a runner after settling last. Maybe the soft track contributed so give her another chance on a good deck. MISS LIL (6) returns from a 264-day spell. Form last prep was underwhelming to say the least. Dean Yendall rides for the first time - can play a role if she brings her best form. GUNNATIPPATINNIE (3) is a Kermadec three-year-old on debut. Placed in a recent Geelong jump-out. Won't need to be a star to test this field. PEE PLATER (2) last raced when he worked home well to be beaten under four lengths over 1100m at Ararat in May. Two recent trials should have him up to the mark. DANSEUR NOBLE (1) has won a couple of recent Murray Bridge jump-outs and should give a good account on debut.",
